# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 9 (a host's child document is a dynamic), R7 (rows built after the tick from the values after it) and ch. 7 as ruled (round 3 ST), with the document `$(Path ==> $Elem c)` (Jimmy, 6 November 2026): the label's entry after m is the child's label after m-1 and the flattening `for`'s `$flat` a tick behind that, so a kept row shows the new count with the label two ticks behind, and the moved label in the two owed ticks after.
